chezmoi dots pkg add — Add a package or pinned release to the source

USAGE
  chezmoi dots pkg add <name> [--brew[=<formula>]] [--cask <name>] [--apt[=<package>]] [--winget <id>] [--uv[=<spec>]] [--npm[=<spec>]] [options]
  chezmoi dots pkg add <name> --release --version <v> --url <template> --target <os/arch>=<name>... [options]
  chezmoi dots pkg add <name> --github <owner/repo> [options]

ARGUMENTS
  name  Entry name, letters, digits, - and _.
  Package mode (default) takes the install sources from flags: a bare --brew, --apt, --uv or --npm installs <name>, --brew=<formula> installs that instead.
  Without a source flag the package managers on this machine are asked: brew and cask on macOS, apt on Linux, winget on Windows, uv and npm everywhere. Only this machine is looked at, never a public index; the keys of other OSes come only from flags or from running pkg add there. Detected sources are confirmed one by one on a terminal, else need --yes. Any source flag turns detection off.
  An existing package gets the keys it lacks; keys it has are never changed.
  Release mode (--release) needs --version, --url (with {version}) and one or more --target; it downloads each asset to record its sha256 (--dry-run does not).
  --github reads the latest release of owner/repo (GH_TOKEN or GITHUB_TOKEN raise the rate limit) and proposes the entry from its asset names: darwin, linux and windows on amd64 and arm64 are recognized, checksums, signatures and installers are left out, archives win over bare binaries, a tie is reported as ambiguous. The proposal needs a yes on a terminal, else --yes; --dry-run still reads GitHub but downloads no archive.
  The entry is added to .chezmoidata/packages.toml, which is validated afterwards, then staged, committed and pushed alone as far as the chezmoi git settings ask. An existing release is never changed.

OPTIONS
  -h, --help  Show this help and exit successfully.
  --apt  install with apt; --apt=<package> when the package differs from the name (default: "")
  --brew  install with brew; --brew=<formula> when the formula differs from the name (default: "")
  --cask <name>  install with brew cask name (default: "")
  --dry-run  print the entry, write nothing and download no archive (default: "false")
  --github <owner/repo>  add a release from the latest GitHub release of owner/repo (default: "")
  --npm  install with npm; --npm=<spec> when the spec differs from the name (default: "")
  --release  add a pinned release binary instead of a package (default: "false")
  --requires <answer>  install only when this [data] answer is set (default: "")
  --roles <roles>  limit to roles (comma list of personal, work, light) (default: "")
  --target <os/arch=name>  repeatable release os/arch=name target (default: "")
  --url <template>  release download template with {version} (and {target}) (default: "")
  --uv  install with uv tool; --uv=<spec> when the spec differs from the name (default: "")
  --version <version>  release version to pin (default: "")
  --winget <id>  install with winget id (default: "")
  --yes  accept the detected sources or the GitHub proposal without asking (default: "false")

ENVIRONMENT
  CHEZMOI_EXECUTABLE  chezmoi executable (default: chezmoi).
  CHEZMOI_CONFIG_FILE  chezmoi config file (default: chezmoi's config).
  CHEZMOI_SOURCE_DIR  source directory (default: ask chezmoi; honors .chezmoiroot).
  GH_TOKEN / GITHUB_TOKEN  optional token for --github.

EXAMPLES
  chezmoi dots pkg add wget --brew --apt
  chezmoi dots pkg add wget
  chezmoi dots pkg add example-app --cask example-app --roles personal
  chezmoi dots pkg add example-tool --release --version 1.2.3 --url https://example.com/{version}/tool-{target}.tar.gz --target linux/amd64=linux-x86_64
  chezmoi dots pkg add example-tool --github octocat/example-tool --dry-run
